{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 40, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "My recent trip to Japan was a mesmerizing blend of ancient tradition and futuristic innovation. From the moment I stepped off the plane in Tokyo, the energy was electric. The neon lights of Shibuya Crossing seemed to pulse with life, contrasting sharply with the serene silence of the Fushimi Inari Shrine in Kyoto, where thousands of vermilion torii gates wind up the mountain.\n\nOne of the highlights was experiencing the seamless efficiency of the Shinkansen. Gliding between cities at 300 km/h, I watched the countryside blur into a watercolor of green fields and snow-capped mountains. It felt like traveling through time and space simultaneously.\n\nCulinary discovery was another pillar of the journey. I savored fresh sushi at a tiny counter in Tsukiji Market, where the chef's precision was as impressive as the taste. A steaming bowl of ramen in a narrow alleyway in Osaka warmed my soul on a chilly evening, while delicate matcha sweets in a traditional tea house offered a moment of peaceful reflection.\n\nBeyond the sights and flavors, it was the warmth of the people that left the deepest impression. A simple \"arigato gozaimasu\" was met with genuine smiles and polite bows. The concept of *omotenashi*, or wholehearted hospitality, is woven into the fabric of daily life there.\n\nAs I boarded my flight home, I realized Japan isn't just a destination; it's an experience that reshapes your perspective. The harmony between the old and the new, the quiet and the loud, creates a unique rhythm that is impossible to forget. I am already counting down the days until my next visit to this incredible island nation.", "logprobs": [{"token": "My", "logprob": -2.0766354}, {"token": " recent", "logprob": -0.05974687}, {"token": " trip", "logprob": -0.99869466}, {"token": " to", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -5.960466e-07}, {"token": " was", "logprob": 